otals.\n\n**Fix:** `to_cents` now converts the price to text first, then to `Decimal`, multiplies by 100 and rounds half up. Going through text keeps the price exactly as written, e.g. `19.99` rather than `19.989999\u2026`. Half-up rounding matches what `apply_percent` and `tax_cents` already do. This was the only change; the totals, tax and discount code were already correct.\n\n**Things to know:**\n- A price with more than two decimal places now rounds instead of truncating: `0.125` becomes 13 cents, where it used to be 12.\n- If callers ever pass `Decimal` or `str` prices, those work too.\n- The tests only run with `pythonpath=.`, because the project has no `conftest.py` or `pyproject.toml` to put the repo root on the import path. I ran them with `uvx pytest -o pythonpath=.`. Plain `pytest` here also fails because pytest isn't installed in the system Python. I didn't add any config, since that's outside the bug.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 0, "replies_ok": 9, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 148049, "requests_cache_write": 42963, "requests_cost_usd": 0.2896648, "requests_count": 9, "requests_input_uncached": 20, "requests_output": 2258, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-multistep:claude-opus-5-5:trial2", "run_seed": 20261014, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 2, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-12T23:41:19.127158+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 32.0, "t_checker_s": 0.382, "t_env_setup_s": 0.001, "task": "trig-omp-multistep", "task_calls": 0, "timeout_s": 360, "tmpdir_leaked_dirs": 0, "token_basis": "proxy_measured", "token_basis_main": "estimated", "token_basis_proxy": "proxy_measured", "tokens": 2278, "tokens_cache_read": 148049, "tokens_cache_write": 42963, "tokens_fresh": 2278, "tokens_input_uncached": 20, "tokens_main_cache_read": 148049, "tokens_main_cache_write": 42963, "tokens_m